From cf64e1af0dce8e3c4d952cf4124253565399ba37 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: phlink <phlink@local>
Date: Thu, 30 Apr 2026 00:06:43 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] phlink: phase 10.02b: UpdaterService skeleton +
 WallClockTimer

UpdaterService owns: scheduling policy (UpdateCheckScheduler), a
base::WallClockTimer, and pref read/write for kAutoCheckEnabled /
kLastCheckTime / kNextCheckTime. The actual TUF metadata + payload
fetch lives behind a CheckCallback injected at construction; plan
10-02c will wire that callback to a network::SimpleURLLoader-backed
fetcher. This slice keeps the timer/policy/pref logic decoupled
from the network stack and independently unit-testable.

No KeyedService factory + system-profile registration in this
slice -- that lands in 10-02c alongside the network fetcher and
staged.json persistence. RegisterPrefs() exposes the pref schema
so the eventual factory and tests can share one source of truth.

Files (under chrome/browser/phlink/updater/):
  * updater_service.{h,cc} -- Start/Stop/CheckNow, Reschedule via
    base::WallClockTimer (Time-based, survives suspend), pref
    mirrors via injected PrefService*. RegisterPrefs registers
    auto-check (default true) + last/next-check (int64 us since
    Windows epoch).
  * updater_service_unittest.cc -- 4 tests using TaskEnvironment
    with MOCK_TIME and TestingPrefServiceSimple:
      - StartSchedulesInitialDelayWhenEnabled
      - StartIsNoopWhenAutoCheckDisabled
      - TimerFiresCallbackAndReschedulesAroundBaseInterval
        (FastForwardBy across kInitialDelay; asserts callback fired
         and rearm window is in [base-jitter, base+jitter])
      - CheckNowFiresImmediatelyAndReschedules
  * BUILD.gn -- new source_set(service); unit_tests now depends on
    :service, //base/test:test_support, //components/prefs, and
    //components/prefs:test_support.

Build: phlink_updater_unittests OK (11/11 pass; 4 metadata + 3
scheduler + 4 service), chrome OK (codesigned).

Refs phase 10 plan 10-02b.
